The query in `1result.sql` is the best choice:

• Uses `DENSE_RANK()` so every tied station shares the same rank while the next rank value increases by 1 (cleaner handling of ties than `RANK()`).  
• Filters with `rk <= 15`, guaranteeing that every tied station inside the top‑15 group is included.  
• Computes all four requested fields (station_id, total trips, % of total, average duration) exactly as required.  
• Joins only once to the stations table and employs clear, concise CTEs.

